{"question_text": {"৫১তম স্পেশাল বিসিএস [স্বাস্থ্য] - ডেন্টাল অংশ": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) A dentist publishes a false written statement that damages another dentist's reputation. Which form of defamation is most appropriate?", "option1": "Slander", "option2": "Libel", "option3": "Assault ", "option4": "Battery", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><strong>DEFAMATION</strong><br>Defamation can be defined as the publication of false statement which lowers the reputation of a person in the eyes of right-thinking members of society generally.For the statement to be actionable as defamatory in English law.<br>1. It has to be broadcasted<br>2. Have no lawful justification.<br>3. It should be made the object of discrediting the person concerned or exposing him to hatred, contempt or ridicule.<br>Types of defamation:Defamation is of two types:<br>• 1. Libel: When statement is in permanent form e.g. writing, printing, carving, cartoon or film or broadcast on radio or television.<br>• 2.Slander: when statement is in a transitory form e.g. spoken words conveyed by a gesture.</p>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Who is the owner of the dental records?", "option1": "The patient", "option2": "The patient's next of kin", "option3": "The practitioner", "option4": "The police", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Owners of dental record:<br>1. Practitioner concerned.<br>2. In case of employee his employer.<br>3. Hospital.<br>4. Clinic.<br>Following are not owners:<br>1. The patient.<br>2. The kins of the patient.<br>3. The police.<br>4. The ordinary people.</p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) A patient gives the dentist an inaccurate medical history, and this contributes to an adverse outcome. This is best classified as:", "option1": "Criminal negligence", "option2": "Civil negligence", "option3": "Contributory negligence", "option4": "Intentional tort", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><strong>Contributory negligence <br></strong>It is any unreasonable conduct or absence of ordinary care on the part of the patient or his personal attendant, which combined the doctor's negligence.<br>Examples:<br>1. Failure to give the doctor accurate medical history.<br>2. The doctor is required to keep abreast of the times and to ice in accordance with the approved methods practice and means of treatment in general use.<br>3. Doctors should be responsible for the injuries that are result of his acts.<br><strong><br></strong></p>\r\n<p></p>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) ", "option1": "", "option2": "", "option3": "", "option4": "", "answer": "0", "exp": ""}, {"id": "17", "questi